Human: Can you tell me the steps to write an if/then statement in C programming language?

Assistant: Of course.  In C, if/then statements look like this:

	if (condition) {
		// do this
	}

	if (condition) {
		// do this
	}

	if (condition) {
		// do this
	}

This statement will execute the code inside the first block of code if the condition is true, the second block of code if the condition is false, and the third block of code if the condition is neither true nor false.
